sub(31, 'Relays only transport it: a relay\'s bytes either verify — and are then THE value — or fail; a failing, garbled, absent or late relay is RETRY, and a later collection yields the same bytes or nothing.', 'Relays only transport it. What is unique is the SIGNATURE (hence the seed); the BYTES a relay serves are NOT unique — different HTTP encodings (key order, whitespace, extra fields) can carry the same signature — so the code treats a live body by the VALUE it carries: same signature in different bytes = the same value (counted live-confirmed, the representation difference recorded in the verdict); a body that does not verify = transport noise (not counted; RETRY on quorum loss); a DIFFERENT signature that also verifies under the pinned key for R would contradict uniqueness under one key — `REFUSE-CONFLICTING-VALID-SIGNATURES`, a defect of the key, not of a relay. A failing, garbled, absent or late relay is RETRY, and a later collection yields the same value or nothing.')
