sub(37, '**3c. V16 — WHAT EXPEDITING COSTS, WHAT IS PRESERVED, HOW THE ORDER STAYS VISIBLE.** COLLECTION HISTORY, COMPLETE (V19 audit M2): the collector CLI logs EVERY attempt — `--log` is mandatory — including refusals and pre-parse/I-O errors (`collector-collect`, `collector-verify`, `collector-refusal`, `collector-error`); the builder `build_corpus_identity_v20.py` (`f3aa4955c150798fb255d6d9d89217e0872981b09fca6d8e845d2106358d70e0`) logs every path — pre-parse refusals (`builder-pre-parse-refusal`), every verdict, witness/adoption refusals, the first ACCEPT (`builder-accept`, binding) and any conflicting later ACCEPT (`builder-conflict`, then `COLLECTION-LOCKED`) — to the append-only `_optionA_dev/collection_log.jsonl`;',
    '**3c. V21 — WHAT THE AMENDMENT COSTS, WHAT IS PRESERVED, HOW THE ORDER STAYS VISIBLE.** COLLECTION HISTORY, AUTHENTICATED (V19 audit M2; codex V20 M2): `_optionA_dev/collection_log.jsonl` is a hash chain (`corpus_identity/history.py`): the collector CLI (`--log` mandatory) writes the GENESIS on the first collect — anchored to SHA-256(approval record bytes), T_pulse, the rule digest and the round — and refuses to re-initiate an existing history or to log into one initiated for another approval (`HISTORY-EXISTS`, `HISTORY-GENESIS-MISMATCH`); every later entry carries `prev_sha256` of the previous line and a stage from a closed set (`collector-collect`, `collector-verify`, `collector-refusal`, `collector-error`, `witness-pending`, `witness-closed`, `builder-pre-parse-refusal`, `builder-verdict`, `builder-witness-or-adoption`, `builder-error`, `builder-accept`, `builder-conflict`); appends happen under an exclusive file lock after re-validating the chain, and the FIRST ACCEPT is taken ATOMICALLY (`history.append_locked`: read-check-append under one lock, so two racing builders cannot both be first); a deleted, edited, reordered or reset history fails `history.validate` and is refused (`HISTORY-INVALID`), disclosed beside the log (`<log>.pregenesis.jsonl`), never treated as a fresh start; a failure before the genesis inputs exist is written to that sidecar by name. The builder `build_corpus_identity_v21.py` (`048b42211a23f47ee4d97a9f6b7658b169736dbc2c4aa2f922f14dbb9d6a65d0`) requires the collector\'s genesis for THIS approval record and logs every path — pre-parse refusals, every verdict, witness refusals WITH their PENDING/CLOSED state, adoption refusals, the first ACCEPT (binding), conflicts (`builder-conflict`, then `COLLECTION-LOCKED`; a later accept-bearing entry naming a different record or seed is a semantic conflict, refused with or without the label), and ANY other exception (`builder-error`, then `BUILDER-ERROR`);')
